Reading it: a curve decaying toward zero with a small final swing is
a fixed point. A curve that flattens at a non-zero value is a rule
still pushing at convergence, held in place only by the mask; a
large final swing is the oscillation some Graph NCA rules show. The
drift column is the stability claim -- it should stay near zero well
past the length the rule was trained at.

